From 2b66310d79926eefb1b87de51bf6c2f632fb8840 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shengyu Liu <shengyuliu@deepseek.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 22:40:02 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add DeepSeek-V4.1 attention kernels

- Restructure csrc into csrc/kernels (per-architecture / per-operation tree) with
  hierarchical namespaces and a .cpp API layer, and rename MODEL1 to DeepSeek-V4.
- Sync the vendored kerutils library with the upstream version.
- Add the sm100 sparse prefill kernels (h_q = 64 / 128, d_qk = 512 / 576).
- Add the sm100 sparse decode kernel for h_q = 64 with the DeepSeek-V4.1 KV cache
  formats (V41 fp8 and the V41_FP4 extra cache) and the shared dequantization helpers.
- Add the fused norm + RoPE + attn + RoPE + cast operator and its permute kernels.
- Build sm_100a / sm_103a targets and register the new sources.
- Extend the tests with the V4.1 KV cache layouts and the fused kernel test, and
  document the new KV cache formats in the README and the Python API.
